    "traits": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Calcification"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(incapacitation, primal, transmutation)\n\nA blow from a granite glyptodont's tail hardens the flesh of the creature struck. The target must succeed at a DC 26 Fortitude saving throw or become slowed 1 (or slowed 2 on a critical failure). Further failed saves against calcification increase the value of the slowed condition. Once a creature's actions are reduced to 0 by calcification, that creature becomes petrified. If the creature isn't petrified, the slowed conditions end once 1 minute passes without the creature failing a save against calcification.\n\nEvery 24 hours after it was petrified, the creature can attempt a DC 26 Fortitude save to recover. On a success, it becomes flesh again, but is slowed 1 for the next 24 hours. On a critical success, the creature recovers and isn't slowed.\n\nOn a failure, the creature remains petrified, but can try again in 24 hours.\n\nOn a critical failure, the petrification is permanent, and the creature can't attempt any more saves."
            },
            "id": "639f66c9-24c8-49ea-9a75-f8b03a2c7c43",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:26.736825"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Earth Glide"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "A living boulder can Burrow through earthen matter, including rock.\n\nWhen it does so, it moves at its full burrow Speed, leaving no tunnels or signs of its passing."
